## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/output.html
- Summary (EN): The Output node defines where a subnetwork hands its results back to the parent network. It forwards whatever reaches its inputs so the parent can use them as its outputs.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Output renvoie les résultats d'un sous-réseau vers le réseau parent, dans l'ordre de ses entrées.

- Inputs meaning: ["1: first input, becomes the parent subnetwork's first output", "2: second input, becomes the second output", "Each further input maps to the next output, in order"]

- Key parameters: ["No parameters documented on the Output node itself. The Outputs parameter of the parent Subnetwork COP sets the output signature."]

- Caveats: ["Only one Output COP should exist at the same level of a network.", "Inside an HDA, the node signature reflects that of the containing operator."]

